  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "In the circuit image the joystick's five header pins sit in one column of the breadboard (rows j to f) with the wire ends touching them. Those holes are a single strip, so putting the pins in it would short all five pins together. I connected the wires straight to the joystick pins and left the joystick resting on the breadboard (contact edge) instead of inserting its pins.",
   "The image wires pin A0 to the joystick VER pin and A1 to HOR. The schematic agrees, and I used that mapping. The text says the x-axis is on A0, which would mean VERT is x on this module.",
   "The Leonardo's 5V and GND pins go to joystick VCC and GND. GND.1 is used for the single GND wire.",
   "The status LED (pin 5, with a 220 ohm resistor) and the second pushbutton (pin 3, with a 10k pulldown) are optional. The manual only refers to other tutorials for them and no images show them, so they are not in the graph.",
   "The joystick's built-in pushbutton (SEL) goes to pin 6 and needs no external pulldown.",
   "The USB cable to the computer is not drawn in the circuit image, so it is not included."
  ]
 },
